### 2. Use Labelled Agents
Instead of using `agent any`, use labelled agents to ensure that builds are distributed across available nodes. This can help balance the load and prevent queue full errors.

### 3. Optimize Pipeline Configuration
Modify your Jenkinsfile to use parallel stages and ensure that each stage is properly configured to handle the load.

### 4. Use Docker Agents
Using Docker agents can help manage resource allocation more efficiently and ensure that each build runs in an isolated environment.

